              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log in to Microsoft OneDrive, you can access your account through your web browser, desktop application, or mobile device. \n\n### 1. Web Browser (Direct Link)\nThe quickest way to access your files from any device is through the web:\n* **Go directly to the login page:** Click here to **[Sign in to Microsoft OneDrive](https://onedrive.live.com/about/signin/)**.\n* **Steps:**\n  1. Enter the **email address** or **phone number** associated with your Microsoft account (such as @outlook.com, @hotmail.com, or your school/work email).\n  2. Click **Next**.\n  3. Enter your **password** and click **Sign in**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Desktop App (Windows & Mac)\nIf you want your files to sync directly to your computer:\n* **On Windows:**\n  1. Press the **Windows Key** and type **OneDrive**.\n  2. Click on the OneDrive app to open it.\n  3. Enter your Microsoft account email and password to start syncing.\n* **On macOS:**\n  1. Open **Finder**, go to **Applications**, and open **OneDrive** (if it isn't installed, you can download it from the Mac App Store).\n  2. Enter your Microsoft credentials to log in.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Mobile App (iOS & Android)\nTo access your files on your phone or tablet:\n1. Download the free **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the Apple App Store or Google Play Store.\n2. Open the app and tap **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your Microsoft email and password.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Troubleshooting Login Issues\n* **Forgot your password?** On the sign-in screen, click **Forgot password?** or **Can't access your account?** to reset your credentials.\n* **Work or School Accounts:** If you are logging in with an account provided by your job or school, make sure to use your organization's login credentials. You may be redirected to your organization's custom sign-in portal.",
